import SwiftUI
struct ReshapeTableInformationView:View {
    var body:some View {
        VStack(alignment:.leading,spacing:10) {
            LessonTextPanel(title:"Change what one row means",text:"Long turns selected fields into observations. Wide makes fields from observed key values. These operations change the observation population: use them before Partition or fitted preprocessing. Those inputs are refused. If an entity appears on several rows, use group-aware evaluation splitting so related observations do not leak across training and evaluation.")
            LessonTextPanel(title:"Long",text:"Identifier fields repeat on each emitted row. Value-field order controls expansion within each original row; arrows and grips change it. Identifier and value selections must be disjoint. The field-name output identifies the original column; the value output stores its value. Output names cannot collide. Keep emits missing values; Drop omits only that value’s row. Strict requires matching types. Checked numeric widening permits integer/number mixtures only when each integer is exactly representable. Images pass through only in a homogeneous image value field; no image-to-text conversion occurs.")
            LessonTextPanel(title:"Wide",text:"Row keys define one output row; missing row-key values form a group. Column names come from one scalar field. Each ordered value row contributes its prefix plus each observed key label. Maximum output columns includes row keys and is at most 128. First seen follows incoming key order; Sorted uses typed key order with missing labels last. Prefixes and key labels must produce unique, nonblank names. The vocabulary is observed at run time; a working sample cannot establish the full source’s vocabulary.")
            LessonTextPanel(title:"Duplicates and missing values",text:"Repeated row-key/column-key pairs stop by default. Aggregate enables each selected reducer. First and Last follow input order and apply the selected missing-value policy. Counts return integers; Mean returns Number; Sum, Minimum and Maximum preserve type. Sum/Mean require numeric values and refuse overflow. Like Summarize, Skip ignores missing values and an entirely missing group returns missing; Return missing propagates a missing value; Stop run refuses it. Count rows counts all retained rows, and Count nonmissing includes empty text. Missing column-name keys stop, drop their entire source row, or use your explicit label. An unobserved combination becomes missing or the chosen typed fixed fill; this does not replace a missing value within an observed group. One fill must match every output value type. Image values support First, Last and counts; fixed image literals are unavailable.")
            LessonTextPanel(title:"Evidence and limits",text:"Long qualifies each observation by its original identity and source field. Wide records the exact retained membership for each row-key group. Source digests include the full configuration. Long streams; Wide groups in bounded disk scratch. Shared five-million-cell, serialized-byte and scratch budgets apply without a 100,000-row cap. Cancellation discards partial scratch. Search filters these controls only. Apply saves one draft; Revert restores it. Results shows captured output, with complete/working-population authority inherited from upstream demand. View requests complete dependencies.")
        }
    }
}
